Figure 3: KTM5900 Application Circuit Diagram


The application circuit for KTM5900 is shown in Figure 3. This chip requires external sensor input in the form of sine and cosine signals. Compatible sensor types include but are not limited to AMR, TMR, and optical
sensors. When using an AMR sensor, two orthogonal TMR switches can
be connected to differentiate between the front and rear halves of the
AMR signal. After receiving analog input, KTM5900 can convert it into
absolute angle information and transmit it to the control processor HOST
through interfaces such as ABZ, UVW, SPI, and others. Ports P0-P5 can
be programmed as ABZ, UVW, or their differential signals ~ABZ, ~UVW. It
is important to note that the recommended capacitors in the schematic
are necessary for ensuring system accuracy and stability.


