4.5 SPI Angle Output Width Configuration



The width of various signal bits in the SPI output can be customized us- ctrREG ctrREG
ing the S.RCBW and S.AGBW registers. In this case, the total SPI out
put width may not strictly adhere to the standard 32-bit or 40-bit format.
These output signals always start from the Most Significant Bit (MSB), and
if the actual number of bits is less, the system will pad 1’s after the Least
Significant Bit (LSB) to ensure data integrity and consistency.



