in a high-speed stable state, it is recommended to perform the
calibration in such a state to improve the accuracy and speed of
fitting.

##### • [After calibration is complete, the system will use the fitted]

parameters to perform real-time linear calibration. If environmental
factors cause the linear error to change, automatic calibration can
be restarted to update the parameters.

##### • [If the system’s linear error changes slowly, consider keeping the]

automatic calibration mode continuously enabled. In this way, the
system will adjust the fitting parameters in real-time to adapt to
changes in error.



