However, it’s important to note that if the rotation speed exceeds this maximum frequency
limit, the _A_ and _B_ signals will output at the maximum frequency. Additionally, depending
on the settings of the IRQ module, the system may issue an overspeed warning. In such
cases, due to the mismatch between the frequency of _A_ and _B_ and the actual rotation
speed, the angle values obtained from the output of the ABZ module may lag behind the
actual angle values.


This frequency limiting mechanism plays a vital role in ensuring the stability and reliability
of the ABZ signal output. By preventing the _A_ and _B_ signals from exceeding the maximum
frequency, it helps to avoid potential issues caused by signal distortion or processing ctrREG

limitations of the receiving system. Users should carefully set the A.ABL parameter

according to the specific requirements of their application scenario to ensure optimal
performance of the ABZ encoder output.


